{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>And they brought it to the Tent of Meeting, a memorial for the children of Israel</b> – It appears from this that they made service vessels from them and delivered them to the public as a memorial for all the children of Israel, so that they would perform with them the service of HaShem for generations. For if these vessels came to the treasury of the House of HaShem, it would have been fitting to say 'a memorial for them before HaShem,' for 'the children of Israel' could include all the people, and a memorial in an enduring thing it is."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:52.943141965Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}